From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tempeste <tempeste@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:24:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] flashnext: --tp 2 collectives and shared decode rounds, each
 behind its own flag

Cheaper --tp 2 collectives (fused reductions, no host poll, LM-head rows in one gather, a rank's own MoE slots,
the shared partial summed in place, a RoCE one-shot path for small gathers and sums), wider shared rounds (32 draft
lanes, DeltaNet lane groups, k verify rows a stream), a short last prompt chunk evened out, drafted tokens' n-gram
rows hinted ahead, and two prompt-cache fixes (unfinished requests' newest states evicted last; a kept state keeps
its head format).

Changes, in the order they were made:
- perf(flashnext): --tp 2 collective profile, link bench, partial MoE sum and relaxed prompt flags
- perf(flashnext): a shared round's DeltaNet steps in one launch each, on whole heads and a rank's half (upstream PR
  #1942 by Armin, adapted to a rank's half heads)
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_PREFILL_TAIL evens out a prompt's short last chunk (single-Spark recipe 0013)
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_AHEAD hints a shared round's drafted tokens' n-gram rows (single-Spark recipe
  0013)
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_HEAD_ONCE gathers a pass's LM-head rows in one collective
- test(flashnext): the model, window and fidelity rank tests take TF_RANK_HOST too, so two hosts need no ssh tunnel
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_FUSE_REDUCE=1|2 cuts --tp 2 collectives from 4 to 3 or 2 a layer
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_ASYNC_COLL=1 drops the host poll after every --tp 2 collective
- fix(flashnext): the ASYNC_COLL guard claims the call it judged before exiting, so a verdict about a finished call or
  a shutdown never ends the process
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_LANES=32 and TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_LANE_GROUPS=1 remove two 16-stream cliffs
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUND_ROWS_PER_STREAM=k lets a drafting round verify k rows a stream up to 128
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_MOE_OWN=1 sums only a rank's own MoE slots and drops the y clear
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SHARED_SLOT=1 sums the shared partial where the down projection wrote it (upstream
  #1792's idea)
- fix(prompt-cache): TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_LIVE=1 evicts unfinished requests' newest states last
- fix(flashnext): the head-format boundary behind the 143-151k RestoreRejected band; TF_FLASHNEXT_RESTORE_HEAD_KV=1
  keeps a kept state's head format
- perf(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_ROCE=1 sends the --tp 2 gathers and fp32 sums that fit through the RoCE one-shot
  exchange, sums as one IEEE add in rank order (NCCL's bytes); flashnext-roce checks it against NCCL on two ranks
- test(flashnext): the hand-built collective owners in the host tests start without RoCE

Flags this patch adds (a flag's default is its unset value; unset leaves the engine as it was
before the flag, and a knob named under another flag only matters when that flag is on):
- TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_AHEAD=1 (single-Spark recipe 0013 on these hints): a shared round's drafted tokens' n-gram rows
  are hinted while the head drafts the next, so the verify pass's gather finds them read.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFT_LANES=<n> (2 to 32; unset: 16): the most drafting streams of a shared round whose MTP head runs
  as one batched pass a step (cuda_lanes_draft.batched).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_LANES=0: a shared pass's DeltaNet steps a lane at a time (default: one launch a step).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_LANE_GROUPS=1: a shared pass of more lanes than one DeltaNet lane table holds (16) runs the
  one-launch steps (TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_LANES) once a group of up to 16 lanes, instead of five launches a lane a layer.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PCACHE_LIVE (a family's cache_live): each unfinished request's newest state is pinned (pins) and goes
  only after every superseded and idle state.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_PREFILL_TAIL=rows: a prompt's last chunk under this many rows is evened out with the one before it (0,
  unset or unparsable: off, the single-Spark recipe's default).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_RESTORE_HEAD_KV=1: a drafting stream that restores a kept state takes the format of that state's MTP
  head cache when it differs from the one its length would pick (mtp.headFormatIn: bf16 up to about 79% of the window
  at nvfp4, the main format p...
- TF_FLASHNEXT_ROUND_ROWS_PER_STREAM=<k> (2 to 4; unset or 0: off): a drafting round's rows at most are k a stream,
  from the 64 a round always takes up to 128 (round_rows_max), instead of 64 whatever the streams.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_ASYNC_COLL: a blocking communicator's host calls return only once NCCL has enqueued (or, the first
  time a path is used, connected to the peer), so nothing polls them.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_FUSE_REDUCE=<level> (--tp 2 with the dense split): fewer collectives a layer by summing partial
  products where two exchanges feed the same residual add.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_HEAD_ONCE=1 (--tp 2): a pass's LM-head rows cross the ranks in one gather and are put back in row
  order on the device (cuda_batch_head.projectHead), instead of one gather a row.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_MOE_OWN=1 (--tp 2, with TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_MOE_PARTIAL=1 and TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_FUSE_REDUCE >= 1): the
  partial sum reads only this rank's slots (fn_moe_sum_own), so the n x 11 x 2560 fp32 clear of y before the experts
  goes.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_MOE_PARTIAL=1 (--tp 2): each rank sums its own routed slots and its shared columns into one fp32 row
  and the ranks add those rows (n x 2560 fp32), instead of adding every slot's row (n x 11 x 2560).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_PROFILE=N: every N host boundaries (finish), each site's collectives a boundary on stderr: calls,
  bytes this rank contributes, GPU time from the stream reaching the collective to its end (the peer's lateness and
  the link), host time in the c...
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_PROMPT_RELAXED=1 (--tp 2): prompt passes take the relaxed prompt paths one rank takes by default
  (TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_MX128 tiles, TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_HC2) on each rank's half heads.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_ROCE: the gathers and fp32 sums that fit go by one-shot RDMA writes (openRoce).
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_ROCE_MAX_KB=<KiB> (1 to 65536; unset: 4096, GLM's TF_ROCE_MAX_KB default): the largest collective a
  rank sends by RoCE.
- TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SHARED_SLOT=1 (--tp 2, with TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_MOE_PARTIAL=1 and TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_FUSE_REDUCE >= 1): the
  partial sum reads the shared down projection's fp32 rows where they were written (fn_moe_sum_slot), so their copy
  into y's shared slot goes...
