+/// range's targets start at 2 * lo * half >= hi * half, past every row not yet moved, so no launch reads what another
+/// (or itself) has written. Row 0 stays.
+fn spreadSteps(n: usize, out: *[max_spread_steps][2]usize) []const [2]usize {
